# Netlify routing for PKFIT.
#
# Precedence (Netlify): a matching STATIC FILE is served before any rule here,
# UNLESS the rule is forced with "!". Among rules, first match wins. So static
# marketing pages (/proof -> proof.html, /workbook -> workbook.html, etc.) and
# the built SPA shells (/apply -> apply.html) resolve automatically; the rules
# below only cover paths with no static file of their own.
#
# Layout after the marketing-port:
#   - Marketing site = static HTML at the publish root (home.html, proof.html,
#     about.html, field-notes.html, diagnostic.html, group.html, workbook.html).
#   - React SPA = two shells (app.html, apply.html) that boot the same app.
#     It is only reachable on the LIVE FUNNEL surfaces below. The retired
#     dashboard routes are never served a shell, so the app never boots there.

# --- Server functions (force over everything) ---
/api/webhooks/stripe-audit   /.netlify/functions/stripe-audit-webhook   200!

# --- Live funnel surfaces: must boot the React SPA ---
# /apply has its own static shell (apply.html, apply-specific OG tags) and
# resolves as a static file; listed here for clarity / belt-and-suspenders.
/apply         /apply.html   200
/qualifier     /app.html     200
# The Diagnose agent — five keyword landing surfaces + the canonical path.
/standard      /app.html     200
/structure     /app.html     200
/system        /app.html     200
/protocol      /app.html     200
/align         /app.html     200
/diagnose      /app.html     200
# Legal pages live inside the React app.
/legal/*       /app.html     200

# --- Marketing home ---
/              /home.html    200

# --- Everything else (incl. retired dashboard paths) -> marketing home ---
# Not forced: real static files (/proof, /about, /workbook, assets, etc.) still
# win first. This only catches unknown/retired paths like /dashboard, /coach.
/*             /home.html    200
